  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "pH unadjusted"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients except KP buffer, vitamin solution, Na2CO3 and Na2S·9H2O. Dispense the medium into suitable culture vessels under a stream of H2/CO2 (80/20) and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Separately autoclave KP buffer and Na2S·9H2O (5% solution) under a N2 atmosphere. Sterilize vitamin and 10% Na2CO3 solutions by filtration. Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add KP buffer, vitamin, Na2CO3 and Na2S·9H2O solutions. Pressurize the inoculated vessels to 150 kPa with H2/CO2 (80/20)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Autoclaved under N2."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "First dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with NaOH, and then add minerals. Final pH 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
